  "body": "@treeDweller98 on Linux you can easily install Imagemagick and call it from ART's user commands to create borders. I've posted an example on the French ART forum:\n\nhttps://forum.artherapee.fr/t/creation-bordures/1531/18?u=sguyader\n(outputs images as a jpeg, and adds borders as number of pixel values around)\nand \nhttps://forum.artherapee.fr/t/creation-bordures/1531/25?u=sguyader\n(outputs images as a 16-bit tiff, and adds borders as % of the width and height)\n\nUse google translate or something else to translate to your favorite language if you need to understand the text surrounding the example scripts.\n\nYou may want to specify two commands to accommodate both portrait and landscape orientations.\n\nHope this helps.",
